WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.221
"Is Aging a Disease?"

00:00:07.265 --> 00:00:10.440
For decades, one of the most
contested questions

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:14.100
in gerontology has been
whether or not aging itself

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.020
should be considered a disease.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.920
But aging is natural,
the counterargument goes,

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.360
so it can't be a disease.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.300
Yes, but so is getting
an infection,

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.740
and we call that a disease.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.440
But aging is universal.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.380
Yes, but everybody
gets the common cold, too.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.840
If you ask people
whether they think

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.280
a variety of conditions
should be

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.460
classified as diseases,
you get an odd mix.

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.480
For example, alcohol dependence
is considered a disease,

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.060
but nicotine dependence is not.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.240
Interestingly,
the lay public is more likely

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.940
to view aging as a disease
than doctors,

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.520
despite medicine's
historical penchant

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:55.260
to medicalize everything.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.320
Who could forget drapetomania,

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.540
the mental "illness"

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.000
afflicting slaves
who escaped plantations.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.700
Masturbation
was considered a disease,

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:08.580
complete with
grizzly surgical solutions.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.700
Homosexuality was
officially labeled a disease

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.460
within my lifetime,
yet medicine is hesitant

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.080
to label aging an ailment.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.680
What does it matter
what we call it?

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:22.560
A rose by any other name
wilts just as fast.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.460
The hope is that
disease classification

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.680
would lead to
greater resource allocation

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:29.760
for aging research,

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:34.020
just as the recent declaration
of obesity as a disease did

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.280
for obesity research.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:39.060
Aging is arguably
one of the most important

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.440
unsolved problems of humanity,
yet less than 0.1 percent

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.540
of the National Institutes
of Health budget

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:48.300
is spent on understanding
the aging process.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:52.380
Even though aging
may be the leading cause

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.520
of disease and death,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.760
only 4 out of 14
general medicine textbooks

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.080
have a chapter on the subject,

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:01.620
and 5 of 14 didn't appear
to address aging at all.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:04.860
The science of aging
appears to have been

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.900
"relegated to a limbo

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.940
reserved for
impractical projects

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.120
or eccentric whims
not quite worthy

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:14.220
of serious
scientific consideration.”

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:19.680
Why doesn't Big Pharma invest
in what would certainly be

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.760
a blockbuster drug?

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:24.960
Why spend the money on research
when it can be spent

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.900
marketing all the unproven
anti-aging products

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.160
they already sell?

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:32.220
Many of the leading lines
of dietary supplements

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.780
are owned by drug companies.

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.780
They're the ones selling
"cosmeceuticals"

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.120
and "age reverse" skin creams.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:42.600
Drug maker Sanofi even partnered
with Coca-Cola

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.340
to come up with
a "beauty drink."

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.120
They're already making money
hand over fist

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.880
preying on the public's
gullibility and desperation

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.380
for anti-aging products.

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:55.020
Why waste valuable
marketing money

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.720
on proving anything
actually works?

